.TH QTGRASS 1 "2026-05-14" "qtgrass 0.1.0" "GRASS GIS Qt6 GUI"
.SH NAME
qtgrass \- Qt6 native graphical user interface for GRASS GIS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtgrass
[\fB\-\-module\fR \fIMODULE\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
[\fB\-\-qtui\-cmd\fR \fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qtgrass
is a full-featured Qt6 replacement for the GRASS GIS wxPython GUI.
It provides an integrated environment for running GRASS modules,
visualising raster and vector data, and performing spatial analyses.
.PP
When invoked without arguments,
.B qtgrass
opens the full GUI: startup wizard (location/mapset selection), map canvas,
module toolbox, layer panel, and all tool dialogs.
.PP
When invoked with
.BR \-\-module ,
a standalone module dialog is opened for the named GRASS module and the
program exits when the dialog is closed.
.PP
When invoked with
.BR \-\-qtui\-cmd ,
the
.I COMMAND
string (as produced by
.IR G_recreate_command (3))
is parsed into a module name and arguments, and the corresponding module
dialog is shown.  This mode is used by the GRASS
.B \-\-qtui
flag in
.BR parser.c .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-module " MODULE " [\fIKEY=VALUE\fR...]
Open a standalone module dialog for
.I MODULE
with optional pre\-filled parameters.
.TP
.BI \-\-qtui\-cmd " COMMAND"
Parse
.I COMMAND
and show its module dialog.  Used internally by the GRASS
.B \-\-qtui
hook.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GISBASE
Path to the GRASS installation
.RI ( /usr/local/grass86
by default at build time).
.TP
.B GISRC
Path to the GRASS session resource file.
Must point to a valid GRASS environment when running any module.
.TP
.B GRASS_PYTHON
Python interpreter used when spawning GRASS Python scripts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/qtgrass/qtgrass.conf
Per\-user settings (last mapset, window geometry, render mode).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the full GUI:
.PP
.RS
.B qtgrass
.RE
.PP
Open a standalone r.slope.aspect dialog with a pre\-filled map:
.PP
.RS
.B qtgrass \-\-module r.slope.aspect elevation=dem
.RE
.PP
The GRASS
.B \-\-qtui
flag triggers:
.PP
.RS
.B r.slope.aspect \-\-qtui elevation=dem slope=slope
.RE
which is equivalent to running:
.RS
.B qtgrass \-\-qtui\-cmd "r.slope.aspect elevation=dem slope=slope"
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grass (1),
.BR r.slope.aspect (1),
.BR v.net.path (1)
.PP
GRASS GIS project: <https://grass.osgeo.org>
